          "type": "online_environment",
          "definition": "The action domain is $[0,1]^d$. The Matern kernel $k=k_{\\nu,\\ell}$ is public, with smoothness $\\nu>0$, length scale $\\ell>0$, and $k(x,x)=1$. The environment fixes all reward functions before interaction: $$f_t\\in\\mathcal H_k,\\qquad \\|f_t\\|_{\\mathcal H_k}\\le B\\quad(t=1,\\ldots,T).$$ $$\\sum_{t=2}^{T}\\|f_t-f_{t-1}\\|_\\infty\\le V_\\infty,\\qquad \\|g\\|_\\infty=\\sup_{x\\in[0,1]^d}|g(x)|.$$"
